{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 40, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "\"the social network\" is a biographical drama film directed by david fincher, released in 2010. the movie is based on the life of mark zuckerberg, the founder of the social networking site facebook, and his journey to create the platform that would change the way people interact with each other.\n\nthe film begins with mark zuckerberg (played by jesse eisenberg), a sophomore at harvard university, who is dumped by his girlfriend, erica albright (played by rachel mina young). this event sparks mark's idea to create a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two harvard students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes an instant hit, but also gets mark into trouble with the university administration.\n\nmark is approached by twin brothers, cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are members of the harvard rowing team and are looking to create a social networking site for harvard students. they enlist mark's help, but he eventually betrays them and creates his own site, \"thefacebook\", which becomes a huge success.\n\nas the site grows in popularity, mark becomes increasingly obsessed with its success and starts to neglect his friends and relationships. he also gets into a lawsuit with the winklevoss twins, who claim that mark stole their idea.\n\nthe film is known for its witty dialogue, clever cinematography, and outstanding performances from the cast. jesse eisenberg shines as mark zuckerberg, capturing his awkwardness, intelligence, and ambition. andrew garfield plays eduardo saverin, mark's friend and co-founder of facebook, with a nuanced performance that brings depth to the character.\n\nthe film's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also noteworthy, adding to the overall mood and atmosphere of the movie. the soundtrack is minimalist and haunting, perfectly capturing the tone of the film.\n\none of the strengths of \"the social network\" is its ability to explore complex themes such as friendship, betrayal, and the consequences of success. the film raises questions about the ethics of social media and the impact it has on our lives.\n\noverall, \"the social network\" is a thought-provoking and engaging film that is both entertaining and informative. it's a must-see for anyone interested in the story behind one of the most influential social media platforms of our time.", "logprobs": [{"token": "\"", "logprob": -0.9773347973823547}, {"token": "the", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " social", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "\"", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -6.556489552167477e-06}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -2.75758695602417}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.01112178061157465}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.12694275379180908}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " david", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -1.609931230545044}, {"token": " released", "logprob": -0.0248067919164896}, {"token": " in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " ", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "201", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ".", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -2.610649426060263e-05}, {"token": " movie", "logprob": -0.0007563352701254189}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.07698216289281845}, {"token": " based", "logprob": -0.00038926175329834223}, {"token": " on", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -1.7881377516459906e-06}, {"token": " life", "logprob": -1.2040324211120605}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": " mark", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " zu", "logprob": -2.7418097943154